                        "glosses": [
                            "An African Pygmy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3883682e-61c8-4e9d-b9c5-5f8d18565766",
                                "sense_id": "eb8528a8-45a9-3b18-8e1d-78dae8ff1a2e",
                                "text": "Negrillo children are sometimes caught and held in slavery; but when “they attain the age at which the Spanish laws set them free, they, with but a single known exception, return to the woods.[…]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78a1833b-d6fa-4e60-99ad-183909804cc6",
                                "sense_id": "eb8528a8-45a9-3b18-8e1d-78dae8ff1a2e",
                                "text": "Negrillo Race. — An Aramanga Lad. “THE Negrillo race,” says Dr. Pickering, “has much the same complexion as the Papuan; but differs in the diminutive stature, the general absence of a beard, the projecting of the lower part of the face […]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d6e2b31-d7db-48d5-b58c-336b255ec471",
                                "sense_id": "eb8528a8-45a9-3b18-8e1d-78dae8ff1a2e",
                                "text": "These clicks are very characteristic of the Bushmen and dwarf languages, and if the statement be true, then these two tribes must be Negrillo. It rests, however, solely on some remarks by Tutschek, and is improbable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db6720ef-abf7-44a9-97d3-dc3d91537c66",
                                "sense_id": "eb8528a8-45a9-3b18-8e1d-78dae8ff1a2e",
                                "text": "(v) Negrillo (African pygmy). The Negrillos are very short in stature. Their average height is 4' 6\" or 136 cm. They have short trunk, short legs and long arms; Steatopygea is occasionally present in women."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
